{title: Who Has Believed?}
{artist: Larry Holder / Elton Smith}
{time: 4/4}
{key: C#m}
{tempo: 112}

Verse 1
[C#]Who has believed
[C#]All [F#m7]that we have [F#m]heard,
[F#]Of [G#7]the blessed news that [G#7]now [G#]we [C#]bring?
[C#m]To whom [C#]is revealed
[C#m]The [C#]coming [F#m]of Messiah,
[G#]Coming [G#7]of our Lord [G#]and [C#m]King?
[C#]For He [C#m]has borne our [G#7]grief,
And known [F#m7]our sin and pain,
[G#]Was [A]bruised [F#m7]for all [F#m]our [C#m]iniquity,
By [B]His sacrifice, [G#]set the [C#m]captive free,
That [F#m7]w-e ma-y [G#7]live [C#m]again!

Verse 2
[C#m]He was despised,
[C#7]Rejected [F#m]by His own,
Who, like sheep, [G#]had all been [G#7]led astray.
[C#m]He was oppressed,
Yet He [F#m]opened not His [F#m7]mouth
[F#]As in [G#7]judgement He was led away.
[C#]And He [C#m]who knew no sin
[G#]Received [F#m]our [F#m7]guilt and [G#]pain;
In [F#m]sacrifice, His life [C#m]laid [C#]down,
That in [B]righteousness would [G#7]our souls [C#m]be found,
[C#m7]That w-e [F#m]ma-y live [C#m]again!

Verse 3
[C#m]Who has [C#]believed
[C#m]All [F#m]that we have heard,
[A]Of [G#]the blessed news that now [G#]we [C#m]sing?
Praise to the Lord,
[F#m]Redeemer and Messiah,
[G#7]Everliving [G#]Lord [G#7]and [C#]King!
[C#]His [C#m]soul is satisfied
[G#]By the fruit [F#m]of His [F#m7]travail.
[G#]His [G#]righteous [F#m]kingdom has [C#m]no end;
[C#m]He [E]is [B]our [G#7]Master, [C#]Lord, [C#m]and Friend;
[C#m]His Wo-rd [F#m]wi-ll [G#7]never [C#]fail!
[C#m]{c: Repeat First Chorus}
Yes, He [C#m]has borne [C#m]our [Cm]grief,
[G#]And [D#m7]known [F#m]our sin and [G#7]pain,
[G#7]Was bruised [F#m]for all our [C#m]iniquity,
By His sacrifice, [G#7]set [G#]the captive [C#m]free,
[C#m7]That [G#]w-e [F#m]ma-y live [G#]again!
[C#m]That [C#m]w-e ma-y [C#m]live [E]again!
